        'assert-in': ['Installed', '5.0'],
    },
    # A token the API rejects stops the scanner before it looks at the site. Against a
    # live scanner the scan is repeated without the token, so the exposures still get
    # reported; the fixture path cannot replay two runs, so what is asserted here is
    # that the scanner's own reason survives instead of a generic parsing complaint.
